Rule 1 (mat1 and mat2 must be 2-D matrices)
{v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_3) = 2
>>
Rule 2 (matmul inner dimensions must match)
{v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_3) = 2 ∧ shape(v_2, 1) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 3 (input must be broadcastable to (shape(mat1, 0), shape(mat2, 1)))
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_3, 1)) else if ndim(v_1) = 2 then ((shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)) ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_3, 1))) else false
>>
Rule 4 (mat1 and mat2 must have the same dtype)
{v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 5 (dtype propagation across input, mat1, mat2, and out)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor, v_4: dtype, v_7: tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ v_4 = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_7) = v_4
>>
Rule 6 (out must be a 2-D matrix matching the result shape)
{v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor, v_7: tensor} |= ndim(v_7) = 2 ∧ shape(v_7, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_7, 1) = shape(v_3, 1)
>>
Rule 9 (out must be a Tensor, not a float)
{v_7: tensor} |= ndim(v_7) ≥ 0
